    "body": "### Problem\n\nSimilar to previous issues though this is different because the UI is running on a local _Windows_ client box and the `--headless` server is running on a remote _Windows Server_. Pressing `<c-c>` while in _Terminal_ mode doesn't yield a stopped running `ping internetbeacon.msedge.net -t` or `sleep 30`. This behavior happens in `cmd.exe` and `pwsh.exe`. Workaround is to switch to _Normal_ mode and `:bd`. \n\nWindows to _Ubuntu_ does work. I've tried _Alacritty_ with `zellij`, plain _Alacritty_, _Windows Terminal_, and _wezterm_. These terminal scenarios show the same behavior.\n\nI'm using the modern ConPTY on the aforementioned terminals too. Running `ssh remoteServer` and then running `nvim` does allow `<c-c>` to work in the `:terminal` too.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNOTE: I am using this convuluted method of process starting to breakaway from job. Keep in mind you may need to use a modern version of _OpenSSH_. I install with _chocolatey_ with the below.\n```pwsh\nchoco install openssh --pre --version=9.5.0-beta1 -y --params='\"/SSHServerFeature /SSHAgentFeature /PathSpecsToProbeForShellEXEString:$env:programfiles\\PowerShell\\*\\pwsh.exe\"'\n```\n#### Repro ( NOTE: Need to use the fully qualified path )\n```pwsh\nssh remoteServer '$proc_info = New-CimInstance -CimClass (Get-CimClass -ClassName Win32_ProcessStartup) -Property @{CreateFlags=16777216} -ClientOnly; $arguments = @{CommandLine=\"c:\\users\\user\\scoop\\shims\\nvim.exe --headless --listen 127.0.0.1:8080\"; ProcessStartupInformation=$proc_info}; Invoke-CimMethod -ClassName Win32_Process -Name Create -Arguments $arguments'\nssh -tt -N -L 8080:127.0.0.1:8080 remoteServer\n```\n\n```pwsh\n# In another tab run\nnvim --remote-ui --server 127.0.0.1:8080\n```\n\n```vim\n:terminal\nping 8.8.8.8 -t\n<c-c>\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nExpect to be able to cancel a forever ping.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\nNVIM v0.13.0-dev-1474+gd42367570c\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nN/A\n\n### Operating system/version\n\nWindows 22631.6345 Client / Windows Server 2022 Datacenter\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nAlacritty/wezterm/Windows Terminal\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-256color\n\n### Installation\n\nscoop",
